  "report": {
    "text": "The Sentinel\u20111 analysis shows flood\u2011affected water covering 486.4\u202fkm\u00b2 [E1], which is 1.4\u202fpercent of the observable area [E2]. Permanent water bodies account for 273.5\u202fkm\u00b2 [E3], while the baseline water extent before the event was 8.5\u202fkm\u00b2 [E7], giving a net new water increase of 477.9\u202fkm\u00b2 [E8]. The flood is broken into 154 zones [E4]; the largest zone is 28.97\u202fkm\u00b2 [E5] and overall 65.6\u202fpercent of the flooded area is organised into zones larger than 0.5\u202fkm\u00b2 [E6]. This detection method scores IoU\u202f0.441, precision\u202f0.763 and recall\u202f0.511 on Sen1Floods11 HandLabeled, meaning roughly a quarter of detected pixels may be false positives and about half of true flooding may be missed.",
